# Hovercraft concept update ? 2026-10-29

The supplied reference calls for exposed twin ducted fans, segmented rubber skirt, low glass cockpit, sculpted bodywork and slim lighting. The existing sport hull, cockpit, vents, lighting, paint and livery paths were retained. The forward nacelle fairings were replaced with open diagonal metal braces, exposing each intake and its independently animated blades. Each front guard now has eight spokes and a circular ring. The pressure skirt has 48 molded grooves with matching seams.

The visual revision and baked surface directory were advanced to v4. A native bake verified 314 mesh array round-trips. The hovercraft Garage scene, racing shadow, menu and Garage pictures, 49 livery pictures and news picture were regenerated. Handling and collision sources were not changed. The previous v3 mesh assets remain.

Native Windows Godot 4.7.2 review: Compatibility 28 checks passed including unbatched part checks; desktop Mobile 21 checks passed before the additional part checks were added. Both observed 72,060 full and 22,644 simple triangles. Compatibility actual App Garage and race review passed 10 checks; livery pixel review passed 19 checks; the racing-model and shadow review passed 22 checks. The racing shadow has 1,192 triangles. Captures and mesh provenance are under `docs/evidence/hovercraft-concept-2026-10-29/`. These are desktop checks; device appearance and performance and owner acceptance are outstanding.

The first process-policy launch was rejected, the sandboxed run could not read the Windows certificate store, and the first news bake failed due to incorrect command-line argument formatting. The native runs used isolated `build/hovercraft-concept-review` APPDATA, an empty backend URL and normal access; the corrected news bake passed. The first focused part check ran on batched geometry and failed to find individual nodes; the corrected review disables batching for the inspected model and passes. No owner save, live backend, device, or deployment was used.
